{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766733,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"light-green_un","paid":0,"title":"Hack Into PCell v2.0","festival_id":521740,"organization_id":17467,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-08T00:01:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-30T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/hack-into-pcell-v20-crescendo-fr-conceicao-rodrigues-college-of-engineering-frcrce-bandra-1766733","region":"offline","details":"<p>HACK INTO PCELL v2.0 (Build. Break. Solve.) is a multi-stage technical challenge combining campus exploration, digital puzzles, system investigation, and problem-solving.&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>Teams start with an ESP32-based treasure hunt, discovering checkpoints and cracking clues to progress. The top teams advance to SYSTEM\/\/BREAK, an offline terminal-based challenge where participants investigate a simulated environment, analyze issues, and solve technical challenges via the command line.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility &amp; Team Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team Size: Exactly 3 members per team.<\/li>\n<li>Participation: Open to both Intra-College and Inter-College students.<\/li>\n<li>Inter-College Teams: Allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Inter-Specialization Teams: Allowed (subject to the institutional cap of maximum 2 teams per class).<\/li>\n<li>Class Limit: A maximum of 2 teams are permitted from each class.<\/li>\n<li>First Year (FE) Category: Evaluated separately through Level 1; does not proceed to Level 2. A dedicated FE Winner is selected directly from Level 1 performance.<\/li>\n<li>External Participants: 2 external team slots are reserved for Level 2. An orientation video covering the college layout will be shared one week prior.<\/li>\n<li>Registration Fee: \u20b9200 per team.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Format &amp; Rounds:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Level 1: ESP32 Treasure Hunt\n<ul>\n<li>Date: 29th October 2026<\/li>\n<li>Venue: Room 305 &amp; designated areas (3rd floor and below)<\/li>\n<li>Duration: 1 hour<\/li>\n<li>Number of Checkpoints \/ Problem Statements: Up to 15 physical ESP32 Wi-Fi checkpoints; 15 flag submissions required.<\/li>\n<li>Description: Teams locate physical ESP32 Wi-Fi checkpoints across campus, solve the associated puzzles\/challenges, and submit flags on the event portal.\n<ul>\n<li>Allowed Resources: Smartphones with Wi-Fi capability\/Wi-Fi analyser apps, search engines, AI tools, and the internet are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Advancement: The top 10 regular teams qualify for Level 2.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Level 2: SYSTEM\/\/BREAK\n<ul>\n<li>Date: 30th October 2026<\/li>\n<li>Venue: Room 312<\/li>\n<li>Environment: Controlled, offline terminal-based environment with no internet access.<\/li>\n<li>Focus Areas: Basic Linux commands, system analysis, file hierarchies, logs, processes, network information, permissions, and logical dependencies.<\/li>\n<li>Allowed Resources: A generic SYSTEM\/\/BREAK reference manual will be provided beforehand. Strictly NO internet, NO AI tools, NO search engines, and NO external assistance.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation &amp; Scoring Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Level 1: Ranked primarily by the number of successful flag submissions. Recorded flag completion\/submission time serves as the tiebreaker.<\/li>\n<li>Level 2: Ranked by the number of challenges successfully resolved within the offline terminal environment. Time taken serves as the tiebreaker to determine 1st and 2nd place.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Disqualification Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team Collaboration: Collaboration is strictly limited to registered members of your own team during active rounds.<\/li>\n<li>Fair Play: Any cheating, sabotage, network tampering, unauthorized system access, or sharing information across teams results in immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Disqualification Triggers:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cheating or unauthorized external assistance.<\/li>\n<li>Unauthorized system, network, or restricted physical area access.<\/li>\n<li>Tampering with event infrastructure, checkpoints, or equipment.<\/li>\n<li>Manipulating submission timestamps or exploiting unintended platform bugs.<\/li>\n<li>Unsportsmanlike, disruptive, or unsafe behaviour.<\/li>\n<li>Unauthorized team-member substitutions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Authority: Decisions made by Project Cell organizers and officials are final and binding in all matters.<\/p>","overall_prizes":"Win from a \u20b95,000 cash prize pool, plus certificates and exclusive goodies!","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33503862,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T16:05:18+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-08T00:20:24+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"mOMKoge","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":15,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":0,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-06 16:06:59","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6ac72d2d96de4_whatsapp_image_2026-10-06_at_16_04_33.jpeg","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/150x150\/uploadedManual-6ac72d2d96de4_whatsapp_image_2026-10-